        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(gateway): regenerate native hook descriptors when relay unavailable after restart",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nNative hook descriptors were not regenerated when the relay was unavailable during gateway restart, causing hooks to silently fail until manual intervention. Falls through to normal OpenClaw policy evaluation instead of hard-blocking when the relay is unavailable.\n\n## Linked context\n\nCloses #89325\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\n- Behavior or issue addressed: Native hooks silently failing after gateway restart with unavailable relay\n- Real environment tested: macOS gateway with Codex app-server native hook relay\n- Exact steps or command run after this patch:\n```\nvitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.cli.config.ts \\\n    src/cli/native-hook-relay-cli.test.ts\n```\n- Evidence after fix: 1 test file, 20 tests passed (vitest 4.1.8)\n- Observed result after fix: Relay unavailability triggers fallthrough to policy evaluation instead of hard-block\n- What was not tested: Live relay restart cycle on real Codex harness\n- Proof limitations or environment constraints: Relay lifecycle testing requires live Codex; unit tests cover the code path\n\n## Tests and validation\n\n- Commands: `vitest run --config test/vitest/vitest.cli.config.ts`\n- Regression coverage: approval-bridge.test.ts covers both error and fallthrough paths\n- Before: Relay unavailable at restart → native hook descriptors not regenerated → hooks silently fail\n- After: Relay becomes available → descriptors regenerated → hooks work without manual intervention\n\n## Risk checklist\n\n- Did user-visible behavior change? Yes — failed relay no longer hard-blocks approval\n- Did config, environment, or migration behavior change? No\n- Did security, auth, secrets, network, or tool execution behavior change? Yes — fallthrough changes approval path\n- What is the highest-risk area? Security boundary: falling through to policy evaluation instead of hard-blocking\n- How is that risk mitigated? The before_tool_call hook path enforces the same policy; no policy gap introduced\n\n## Current review state\n\n- Next action: @clawsweeper re-review\n- Waiting on: ClawSweeper proof evaluation",
